{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790970331,"nonce":"rqEGB8T/Tv6oQ6+u8j0pFnnXl9g=","title":"One failing test hides most of the suite in CI","message":"`cargo test` stops after the first test binary that fails, so a single\nfailure suppresses every later binary's results. Measured on this\nworkspace: 84 result lines without `--no-fail-fast`, 295 with it.\n\nThat cost real diagnosis time — a Windows-only panic could not be\nconfirmed fixed because the run aborted before those tests ran, and the\nlog showed one result line for the whole job.\n\n`--no-fail-fast` on the `cargo test` steps would report everything that\nis broken in one run. The nextest steps already continue past a failure;\nthe `cargo test` ones in the Android workflow and the doc-test steps do\nnot.","files":null}]}